  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "decode_frame",
    "file": "ffmpeg/libavcodec/iff.c",
    "description": "decode_frame calls cmap_read_palette() to write a full palette into frame->data[1] for AV_PIX_FMT_PAL8, but it only gates on bits_per_coded_sample <= 8-(mask) and does not ensure the destination palette buffer is large enough for the number of entries cmap_read_palette may write. In cmap_read_palette(), count = 1 << bits_per_coded_sample and the grayscale path writes pal[i] up to count entries (and may duplicate for mask handling), causing out-of-bounds writes when the allocated palette plane is smaller than expected (ASan shows write past a 1103-byte allocation).",
    "conditions": "Trigger with an IFF ILBM/ANIM packet that drives decode_frame into the PAL8 palette initialization path (!s->init, pix_fmt=PAL8) while header/extradata values (notably bits_per_coded_sample/masking/palette offset/size) make cmap_read_palette compute a palette entry count larger than the actual frame->data[1] buffer capacity. The fuzzer input reaches avcodec_send_packet -> decode_frame -> ff_get_buffer (allocates frame buffers) -> cmap_read_palette, where unchecked palette-entry writes overflow heap memory."
  },
